  "correct_label": "Attach Basic {P} Energy → Dreepy (active · 70/70)",
  "frame_key": "86089120|0|decision|14",
  "note": "PROPOSED hold-out, pending the Issue #261 wave-2 verdict. See claims.why — this frame has NOT been user-ruled; the claim states the recommendation and its evidence so the verdict can be given on the diff.",
  "claims": {
    "decision": {
      "correct": [
        1
      ],
      "owner": "#292",
      "why": "PROPOSED HOLD-OUT (Issue #261 POC-T2 item 2e / ADR-0102). NOT yet user-ruled — this is the claim the wave-2 packet asks a verdict on.\n\nWHAT MOVED. ADR-0102 replaced the policy's positional tie-break (the engine's MENU INDEX) with the ADR-0091 fingerprint. Three of the five options attach a Basic Energy onto Dreepy:\n  [1] Basic {P} (cid 5)   score 16.5\n  [2] Basic {D} (cid 7)   score  4.0\n  [3] Basic {R} (cid 2)   score 16.5\n[1] and [3] score EXACTLY equal, so the pick was settled by the tie-break either way. The old index tie-break happened to land on the human's card; the canonical one lands on [3]. Neither tie-break READ anything — the scoring is silent, and this frame's agreement was an accident of menu position.\n\nWHERE THE GAP IS, MEASURED. The attach decider's own working (ADR-0069, shipped ON) on this frame:\n  i=1  energy 5 ({P})   attack_axis 12.5   this_turn 10.0   build 12.5   marginal 15.5\n  i=3  energy 2 ({R})   attack_axis 12.5   this_turn  0.0   build 12.5   marginal 15.5\n`this_turn` separates them and separates them CORRECTLY — Dreepy's Petty Grudge costs {P}, so the {P} attach arms an attack this turn and the {R} attach does not (verified in data/EN_Card_Data.csv: Dreepy — Petty Grudge {P} 10, Bite {R}{P} 40; Dragapult ex — Phantom Dive {R}{P} 200, so BOTH types are on-line and no type gate can split them either). `attack_axis = max(this_turn, build)` then discards it: build is 12.5 for both, this_turn 10.0 is under it, and both marginals come out 15.5.\n\nWHY NOT FIXED IN 2e. Re-composing `attack_axis` prices EVERY attach frame in the corpus — its own swap, its own measurement, its own flip review, materially larger than the ordering item that surfaced it. ADR-0092 also keeps already-built bespoke equations as-is through the POC and forbids answering this with a new rung. Fixing it here would be rung-fitting one frame.\n\nCLAUDE'S RECOMMENDATION: HOLD OUT onto #292. The human's [1] is right and the agent's [3] is wrong, but the defect is in the attach axis, not in the ordering — and the frame was passing for a reason ('option 1 comes before option 3') that was never evidence.\n\nReturns to gating when #292 lands — delete this owner then.\n\nOWNER: #292 (the attach axis takes max(this_turn, build), so an ARMING Energy ties with a merely-building one)."
    }
